WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.989
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.289 --> 00:00:09.536
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.836 --> 00:00:16.621
Unit twenty: Exam Strategies and Study Planning. Today you will plan your study and perform well in university exams.

4
00:00:16.921 --> 00:00:19.411
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:23.948
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:25.761
Revision.

7
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:29.481
Revision means studying again before an exam.

8
00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:31.758
Start revision early.

9
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:35.339
Your turn. Say: Revision.

10
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:38.980
Revision.

11
00:00:39.717 --> 00:00:40.776
Timetable.

12
00:00:41.783 --> 00:00:44.038
Timetable means a plan of times.

13
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.255
Make a study timetable.

14
00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.212
Your turn. Say: Timetable.

15
00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:53.079
Timetable.

16
00:00:53.817 --> 00:00:54.818
Priority.

17
00:00:55.817 --> 00:00:58.072
Priority means something more important.

18
00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:00.033
Set your priorities.

19
00:01:00.617 --> 00:01:03.188
Your turn. Say: Priority.

20
00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:07.081
Priority.

21
00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:09.027
Mock exam.

22
00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:12.388
Mock exam means a practice exam.

23
00:01:12.983 --> 00:01:14.333
Take a mock exam.

24
00:01:14.917 --> 00:01:17.952
Your turn. Say: Mock exam.

25
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:21.975
Mock exam.

26
00:01:22.717 --> 00:01:23.834
Stress.

27
00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.989
Stress means pressure and worry.

28
00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:29.049
Reduce your stress.

29
00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:32.418
Your turn. Say: Stress.

30
00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:36.361
Stress.

31
00:01:37.117 --> 00:01:37.920
Break.

32
00:01:38.917 --> 00:01:40.580
Break means a short rest.

33
00:01:41.183 --> 00:01:42.347
Take a short break.

34
00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:45.254
Your turn. Say: Break.

35
00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:48.857
Break.

36
00:01:49.617 --> 00:01:50.583
Feedback.

37
00:01:51.583 --> 00:01:53.571
Feedback means comments on your work.

38
00:01:54.183 --> 00:01:55.498
Read the feedback.

39
00:01:56.083 --> 00:01:58.794
Your turn. Say: Feedback.

40
00:02:01.633 --> 00:02:02.751
Feedback.

41
00:02:03.517 --> 00:02:04.181
Goal.

42
00:02:05.183 --> 00:02:07.624
Goal means something you want to achieve.

43
00:02:08.217 --> 00:02:09.531
Set a clear goal.

44
00:02:10.117 --> 00:02:12.316
Your turn. Say: Goal.

45
00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:15.808
Goal.

46
00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:20.518
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.383 --> 00:02:23.801
Visal, how do I prepare for exams?

48
00:02:24.917 --> 00:02:33.966
Make a timetable with clear priorities and start revision early. Study in short sessions of about forty minutes and take a break after each one.

49
00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:36.365
How do I practise?

50
00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:46.685
Take mock exams in exam conditions, check your answers and read the feedback. Focus on your weak areas, not only on your strengths.

51
00:02:47.783 --> 00:02:49.493
What about exam day?

52
00:02:50.583 --> 00:03:01.444
Sleep well, arrive early and read each question carefully. Plan your time for each question, write a short outline for essays and check your work at the end.

53
00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.425
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:05.283 --> 00:03:08.572
Grammar focus: Modal verbs for advice.

55
00:03:08.872 --> 00:03:10.024
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:10.717 --> 00:03:12.774
You should start revision early.

57
00:03:13.683 --> 00:03:15.903
Students must read every question.

58
00:03:16.867 --> 00:03:23.374
Use should for advice and must for strong rules: You should start early. You must read every question carefully.

59
00:03:24.117 --> 00:03:27.791
Be careful! Don't say: You should to start early.

60
00:03:29.733 --> 00:03:31.988
Say: You should start early.

61
00:03:32.288 --> 00:03:33.789
No to after should.

62
00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.183
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:37.967 --> 00:03:39.328
Ready for the Exam.

64
00:03:39.628 --> 00:03:42.173
Samnang makes a timetable for the exam month.

65
00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:46.223
He studies in short sessions and takes breaks.

66
00:03:47.233 --> 00:03:49.860
He takes a mock exam and reads the feedback.

67
00:03:50.867 --> 00:03:53.958
He sleeps well and arrives early on exam day.

68
00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:57.837
He plans his time and checks his answers at the end.

69
00:03:58.933 --> 00:04:02.668
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:03.517 --> 00:04:05.458
Revision means studying blank.

71
00:04:05.758 --> 00:04:09.237
A, never. B, less. C, again.

72
00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:14.765
The answer is C: again.

73
00:04:15.917 --> 00:04:17.951
A mock exam is a blank exam.

74
00:04:18.251 --> 00:04:21.963
A, practice. B, final. C, free.

75
00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.337
The answer is A: practice.

76
00:04:28.483 --> 00:04:30.274
Feedback is blank on your work.

77
00:04:30.574 --> 00:04:34.111
A, noise. B, comments. C, money.

78
00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.573
The answer is B: comments.

79
00:04:40.717 --> 00:04:42.914
You should take a blank after a session.

80
00:04:43.214 --> 00:04:46.333
A, test. B, bus. C, break.

81
00:04:49.867 --> 00:04:51.495
The answer is C: break.

82
00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:54.754
When does Samnang check his answers?

83
00:04:55.054 --> 00:04:58.824
A, at the end. B, never. C, at night.

84
00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:04.494
The answer is A: at the end.

85
00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.782
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:09.617 --> 00:05:11.535
How do you prepare for exams?

87
00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:22.222
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:36.891
I make a timetable with clear priorities and start revision early. I study in short sessions with breaks and take mock exams. On exam day I plan my time and check my answers at the end.

89
00:05:37.191 --> 00:05:39.353
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:44.446
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and modal verbs for advice.

91
00:05:44.746 --> 00:05:49.256
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

92
00:05:49.556 --> 00:05:56.751
Congratulations! You have finished Online English for Academic Purposes. See you in Online Writing Skills!

93
00:05:57.051 --> 00:06:00.620
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

